IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc1-support`
IMPORT `ccc1-s7-base`

-- ccc1-s7-persons-and-terrorism.l4 -- section 7, subsections (3) to (3.77): acts or omissions outside Canada against internationally protected persons,
-- hostage taking, torture (s 269.1), United Nations and associated personnel, explosive or other lethal devices, financing of terrorism, terrorism offences
-- and terrorist activity.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30).
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- SHAPE as in ccc1-s7-aircraft-platforms-ships.l4: the lead-in (outside Canada, the kind of offence, the persons or property it is against) is a scope limit: outside it NOTHING;
-- the grounds are an "if" gate: lead-in met and no ground: JUST FALSE. The grounds are a LIST OF constructors named for their paragraphs.
-- Answers of section 2 terms are INPUTS, MAYBE BOOLEAN, carried through when NOTHING: `s 2 internationally protected person`, `s 2 United Nations personnel`, `s 2 associated personnel`,
-- `s 2 terrorism offence`, `s 2 terrorist activity`. "Canadian government or public facility" (ground (g) of (3.72) and similar) uses `s 2 government or public facility`, which never answers
-- NOTHING (PLAN.md section 4): the ground is listed by a caller who has found that the thing is one.

§ `Section 7(3) -- Offence against an internationally protected person`

-- src:414 | Offence against internationally protected person
-- src:415 | (3) Notwithstanding anything in this Act or any other Act, every one who, outside Canada, commits an act or omission against the person of an internationally protected person or against any property referred to in section 431 used by that person that, if committed in Canada, would be an offence against any of sections 235, 236, 266, 267, 268, 269, 269.1, 271, 272, 273, 279, 279.1, 280 to 283, 424 and 431 is deemed to commit that act or omission in Canada if
-- src:416 | (a) the act or omission is committed on a ship that is registered or licensed, or for which an identification number has been issued, pursuant to any Act of Parliament;
-- src:417 | (b) the act or omission is committed on an aircraft
-- src:418 | (i) registered in Canada under regulations made under the Aeronautics Act, or
-- src:419 | (ii) leased without crew and operated by a person who is qualified under regulations made under the Aeronautics Act to be registered as owner of an aircraft in Canada under those regulations;
-- src:420 | (c) the person who commits the act or omission is a Canadian citizen or is, after the act or omission has been committed, present in Canada; or
-- src:421 | (d) the act or omission is against
-- src:422 | (i) a person who enjoys the status of an internationally protected person by virtue of the functions that person performs on behalf of Canada, or
-- src:423 | (ii) a member of the family of a person described in subparagraph (i) who qualifies under paragraph (b) or (d) of the definition internationally protected person in section 2.
@ref s 7(3) (src:414-423)
DECLARE `s 7(3) ground` IS ONE OF
    `s 7(3)(a) the act or omission is committed on a ship that is registered or licensed, or for which an identification number has been issued, pursuant to any Act of Parliament`
    `s 7(3)(b)(i) the act or omission is committed on an aircraft registered in Canada under regulations made under the Aeronautics Act`
    `s 7(3)(b)(ii) the act or omission is committed on an aircraft leased without crew and operated by a person who is qualified under regulations made under the Aeronautics Act to be registered as owner of an aircraft in Canada under those regulations`
    `s 7(3)(c) the person who commits the act or omission is a Canadian citizen or is, after the act or omission has been committed, present in Canada`
    `s 7(3)(d)(i) the act or omission is against a person who enjoys the status of an internationally protected person by virtue of the functions that person performs on behalf of Canada`
    `s 7(3)(d)(ii) the act or omission is against a member of the family of a person described in subparagraph (i) who qualifies under paragraph (b) or (d) of the definition internationally protected person in section 2`

@ref s 7(3) (src:414-423)
GIVEN `the act or omission is committed outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2 internationally protected person: the person against whom the act or omission is committed is one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is against the person of that internationally protected person or against property referred to in section 431 used by that person` IS A BOOLEAN
      offence IS A `Provision of the Code`
      grounds IS A LIST OF `s 7(3) ground`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(3) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the act or omission is committed outside Canada` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every one who, outside Canada, commits an act or omission"
        IF `s 2 internationally protected person: the person against whom the act or omission is committed is one` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is an internationally protected person is the answer of section 2, which was not given
        IF (`s 2 internationally protected person: the person against whom the act or omission is committed is one` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR NOT `it is against the person of that internationally protected person or against property referred to in section 431 used by that person` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "against the person of an internationally protected person or against any property referred to in section 431 used by that person"
        IF NOT `the offence is one of the listed sections` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "would be an offence against any of sections 235, 236, 266, 267, 268, 269, 269.1, 271, 272, 273, 279, 279.1, 280 to 283, 424 and 431"
        IF NOT (null grounds) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is deemed to commit that act or omission in Canada if"
    WHERE
        `the offence is one of the listed sections` MEANS
            `s 7 the offence is in section` offence 235 OR `s 7 the offence is in section` offence 236
            OR `s 7 the offence is in section` offence 266 OR `s 7 the offence is in section` offence 267 OR `s 7 the offence is in section` offence 268 OR `s 7 the offence is in section` offence 269
            OR `s 7 the offence is in section` offence 269.1 OR `s 7 the offence is in section` offence 271 OR `s 7 the offence is in section` offence 272 OR `s 7 the offence is in section` offence 273
            OR `s 7 the offence is in section` offence 279 OR `s 7 the offence is in section` offence 279.1 OR `s 7 the offence is in the range of sections` offence 280 283
            OR `s 7 the offence is in section` offence 424 OR `s 7 the offence is in section` offence 431

§ `Section 7(3.1) -- Offence of hostage taking`

-- src:424 | Offence of hostage taking
-- src:425 | (3.1) Notwithstanding anything in this Act or any other Act, every one who, outside Canada, commits an act or omission that if committed in Canada would be an offence against section 279.1 shall be deemed to commit that act or omission in Canada if
-- src:426 | (a) the act or omission is committed on a ship that is registered or licensed, or for which an identification number has been issued, pursuant to any Act of Parliament;
-- src:427 | (b) the act or omission is committed on an aircraft
-- src:428 | (i) registered in Canada under regulations made under the Aeronautics Act, or
-- src:429 | (ii) leased without crew and operated by a person who is qualified under regulations made under the Aeronautics Act to be registered as owner of an aircraft in Canada under such regulations;
-- src:430 | (c) the person who commits the act or omission
-- src:431 | (i) is a Canadian citizen, or
-- src:432 | (ii) is not a citizen of any state and ordinarily resides in Canada;
-- src:433 | (d) the act or omission is committed with intent to induce Her Majesty in right of Canada or of a province to commit or cause to be committed any act or omission;
-- src:434 | (e) a person taken hostage by the act or omission is a Canadian citizen; or
-- src:435 | (f) the person who commits the act or omission is, after the commission thereof, present in Canada.
@ref s 7(3.1) (src:424-435)
DECLARE `s 7(3.1) ground` IS ONE OF
    `s 7(3.1)(a) the act or omission is committed on a ship that is registered or licensed, or for which an identification number has been issued, pursuant to any Act of Parliament`
    `s 7(3.1)(b)(i) the act or omission is committed on an aircraft registered in Canada under regulations made under the Aeronautics Act`
    `s 7(3.1)(b)(ii) the act or omission is committed on an aircraft leased without crew and operated by a person who is qualified under regulations made under the Aeronautics Act to be registered as owner of an aircraft in Canada under such regulations`
    `s 7(3.1)(c)(i) the person who commits the act or omission is a Canadian citizen`
    `s 7(3.1)(c)(ii) the person who commits the act or omission is not a citizen of any state and ordinarily resides in Canada`
    `s 7(3.1)(d) the act or omission is committed with intent to induce Her Majesty in right of Canada or of a province to commit or cause to be committed any act or omission`
    `s 7(3.1)(e) a person taken hostage by the act or omission is a Canadian citizen`
    `s 7(3.1)(f) the person who commits the act or omission is, after the commission thereof, present in Canada`

@ref s 7(3.1) (src:424-435)
GIVEN `the act or omission is committed outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      offence IS A `Provision of the Code`
      grounds IS A LIST OF `s 7(3.1) ground`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(3.1) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the act or omission is committed outside Canada` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every one who, outside Canada, commits an act or omission"
        IF NOT `s 7 the offence is in section` offence 279.1 THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "would be an offence against section 279.1"
        IF NOT (null grounds) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be deemed to commit that act or omission in Canada if"

-- src:436 | (3.2) to (3.6) [Repealed, 2013, c. 13, s. 3]
@ref s 7(3.2) to (3.6) (src:436-436)
`s 7(3.2) to (3.6) as the text shows them` MEANS "[Repealed, 2013, c. 13, s. 3]"

