§ `Section 7(3.71) -- Offence against United Nations or associated personnel`

-- src:446 | Offence against United Nations or associated personnel
-- src:447 | (3.71) Notwithstanding anything in this Act or any other Act, every one who, outside Canada, commits an act or omission against a member of United Nations personnel or associated personnel or against property referred to in section 431.1 that, if committed in Canada, would constitute an offence against, a conspiracy or an attempt to commit an offence against, or being an accessory after the fact or counselling in relation to an offence against, section 235, 236, 266, 267, 268, 269, 269.1, 271, 272, 273, 279, 279.1, 424.1 or 431.1 is deemed to commit that act or omission in Canada if
-- src:448 | (a) the act or omission is committed on a ship that is registered or licensed, or for which an identification number has been issued, under an Act of Parliament;
-- src:449 | (b) the act or omission is committed on an aircraft
-- src:450 | (i) registered in Canada under regulations made under the Aeronautics Act, or
-- src:451 | (ii) leased without crew and operated by a person who is qualified under regulations made under the Aeronautics Act to be registered as owner of an aircraft in Canada under those regulations;
-- src:452 | (c) the person who commits the act or omission
-- src:453 | (i) is a Canadian citizen, or
-- src:454 | (ii) is not a citizen of any state and ordinarily resides in Canada;
-- src:455 | (d) the person who commits the act or omission is, after the commission of the act or omission, present in Canada;
-- src:456 | (e) the act or omission is committed against a Canadian citizen; or
-- src:457 | (f) the act or omission is committed with intent to compel the Government of Canada or of a province to do or refrain from doing any act.
@ref s 7(3.71) (src:446-457)
DECLARE `s 7(3.71) ground` IS ONE OF
    `s 7(3.71)(a) the act or omission is committed on a ship that is registered or licensed, or for which an identification number has been issued, under an Act of Parliament`
    `s 7(3.71)(b)(i) the act or omission is committed on an aircraft registered in Canada under regulations made under the Aeronautics Act`
    `s 7(3.71)(b)(ii) the act or omission is committed on an aircraft leased without crew and operated by a person who is qualified under regulations made under the Aeronautics Act to be registered as owner of an aircraft in Canada under those regulations`
    `s 7(3.71)(c)(i) the person who commits the act or omission is a Canadian citizen`
    `s 7(3.71)(c)(ii) the person who commits the act or omission is not a citizen of any state and ordinarily resides in Canada`
    `s 7(3.71)(d) the person who commits the act or omission is, after the commission of the act or omission, present in Canada`
    `s 7(3.71)(e) the act or omission is committed against a Canadian citizen`
    `s 7(3.71)(f) the act or omission is committed with intent to compel the Government of Canada or of a province to do or refrain from doing any act`

@ref s 7(3.71) (src:446-457)
GIVEN `the act or omission is committed outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2 United Nations personnel: the person against whom the act or omission is committed is a member of it` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2 associated personnel: the person against whom the act or omission is committed is a member of it` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is against property referred to in section 431.1` IS A BOOLEAN
      offence IS A `Provision of the Code`
      relation IS A `s 7 how the act or omission relates to the offence`
      grounds IS A LIST OF `s 7(3.71) ground`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(3.71) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the act or omission is committed outside Canada` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every one who, outside Canada, commits an act or omission"
        IF `the lead-in against persons or property` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is a member of United Nations personnel or associated personnel is the answer of section 2, which was not given
        IF `the lead-in against persons or property` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "against a member of United Nations personnel or associated personnel or against property referred to in section 431.1"
        IF NOT `the offence is one of the listed sections` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "section 235, 236, 266, 267, 268, 269, 269.1, 271, 272, 273, 279, 279.1, 424.1 or 431.1"
        IF relation EQUALS `s 7 the act or omission has none of those relations to the offence` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "would constitute an offence against, a conspiracy or an attempt to commit an offence against, or being an accessory after the fact or counselling in relation to an offence against"
        IF NOT (null grounds) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is deemed to commit that act or omission in Canada if"
    WHERE
        `the lead-in against persons or property` MEANS
            `ccc1 either of` (`ccc1 either of` `s 2 United Nations personnel: the person against whom the act or omission is committed is a member of it` `s 2 associated personnel: the person against whom the act or omission is committed is a member of it`) (`ccc1 a fact as an answer` `it is against property referred to in section 431.1`)
        `the offence is one of the listed sections` MEANS
            `s 7 the offence is in section` offence 235 OR `s 7 the offence is in section` offence 236
            OR `s 7 the offence is in section` offence 266 OR `s 7 the offence is in section` offence 267 OR `s 7 the offence is in section` offence 268 OR `s 7 the offence is in section` offence 269
            OR `s 7 the offence is in section` offence 269.1 OR `s 7 the offence is in section` offence 271 OR `s 7 the offence is in section` offence 272 OR `s 7 the offence is in section` offence 273
            OR `s 7 the offence is in section` offence 279 OR `s 7 the offence is in section` offence 279.1
            OR `s 7 the offence is in section` offence 424.1 OR `s 7 the offence is in section` offence 431.1

§ `Section 7(3.72) -- Offence involving explosive or other lethal device`

-- src:458 | Offence involving explosive or other lethal device
-- src:459 | (3.72) Notwithstanding anything in this Act or any other Act, every one who, outside Canada, commits an act or omission that, if committed in Canada, would constitute an offence against, a conspiracy or an attempt to commit an offence against, or being an accessory after the fact or counselling in relation to an offence against, section 431.2 is deemed to commit that act or omission in Canada if
-- src:460 | (a) the act or omission is committed on a ship that is registered or licensed, or for which an identification number has been issued, under any Act of Parliament;
-- src:461 | (b) the act or omission is committed on an aircraft
-- src:462 | (i) registered in Canada under regulations made under the Aeronautics Act,
-- src:463 | (ii) leased without crew and operated by a person who is qualified under regulations made under the Aeronautics Act to be registered as owner of an aircraft in Canada under those regulations, or
-- src:464 | (iii) operated for or on behalf of the Government of Canada;
-- src:465 | (c) the person who commits the act or omission
-- src:466 | (i) is a Canadian citizen, or
-- src:467 | (ii) is not a citizen of any state and ordinarily resides in Canada;
