§ `Section 7(3.74) -- Terrorism offence committed outside Canada`

-- src:485 | Terrorism offence committed outside Canada
-- src:486 | (3.74) Notwithstanding anything in this Act or any other Act, every one who commits an act or omission outside Canada that, if committed in Canada, would be a terrorism offence, other than an offence under section 83.02 or an offence referred to in paragraph (a) of the definition terrorist activity in subsection 83.01(1), is deemed to have committed that act or omission in Canada if the person
-- src:487 | (a) is a Canadian citizen;
-- src:488 | (b) is not a citizen of any state and ordinarily resides in Canada; or
-- src:489 | (c) is a permanent resident within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act and is, after the commission of the act or omission, present in Canada.
@ref s 7(3.74) (src:485-489)
DECLARE `s 7(3.74) ground` IS ONE OF
    `s 7(3.74)(a) the person is a Canadian citizen`
    `s 7(3.74)(b) the person is not a citizen of any state and ordinarily resides in Canada`
    `s 7(3.74)(c) the person is a permanent resident within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act and is, after the commission of the act or omission, present in Canada`

@ref s 7(3.74) (src:485-489)
GIVEN `the act or omission is committed outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2 terrorism offence: the act or omission would be one if committed in Canada` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it would be an offence under section 83.02 or an offence referred to in paragraph (a) of the definition terrorist activity in subsection 83.01(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      grounds IS A LIST OF `s 7(3.74) ground`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(3.74) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the act or omission is committed outside Canada` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every one who commits an act or omission outside Canada"
        IF `s 2 terrorism offence: the act or omission would be one if committed in Canada` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the act or omission would be a terrorism offence is the answer of section 2, which was not given
        IF `s 2 terrorism offence: the act or omission would be one if committed in Canada` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "would be a terrorism offence"
        IF `it would be an offence under section 83.02 or an offence referred to in paragraph (a) of the definition terrorist activity in subsection 83.01(1)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "other than an offence under section 83.02 or an offence referred to in paragraph (a) of the definition terrorist activity in subsection 83.01(1)"
        IF NOT (null grounds) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is deemed to have committed that act or omission in Canada if the person"

§ `Section 7(3.75) -- Terrorist activity committed outside Canada`

-- src:490 | Terrorist activity committed outside Canada
-- src:491 | (3.75) Notwithstanding anything in this Act or any other Act, every one who commits an act or omission outside Canada that, if committed in Canada, would be an indictable offence and would also constitute a terrorist activity referred to in paragraph (b) of the definition terrorist activity in subsection 83.01(1) is deemed to commit that act or omission in Canada if
-- src:492 | (a) the act or omission is committed against a Canadian citizen;
-- src:493 | (b) the act or omission is committed against a Canadian government or public facility located outside Canada; or
-- src:494 | (c) the act or omission is committed with intent to compel the Government of Canada or of a province to do or refrain from doing any act.
@ref s 7(3.75) (src:490-494)
DECLARE `s 7(3.75) ground` IS ONE OF
    `s 7(3.75)(a) the act or omission is committed against a Canadian citizen`
    `s 7(3.75)(b) the act or omission is committed against a Canadian government or public facility located outside Canada`
    `s 7(3.75)(c) the act or omission is committed with intent to compel the Government of Canada or of a province to do or refrain from doing any act`

@ref s 7(3.75) (src:490-494)
GIVEN `the act or omission is committed outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the class of offence the act or omission would be if committed in Canada` IS A `Class of offence`
      `s 2 terrorist activity: the act or omission would also constitute a terrorist activity referred to in paragraph (b) of the definition terrorist activity in subsection 83.01(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      grounds IS A LIST OF `s 7(3.75) ground`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(3.75) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the act or omission is committed outside Canada` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every one who commits an act or omission outside Canada"
        IF `the class of offence the act or omission would be if committed in Canada` EQUALS `an offence punishable on summary conviction` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "would be an indictable offence"
        IF `s 2 terrorist activity: the act or omission would also constitute a terrorist activity referred to in paragraph (b) of the definition terrorist activity in subsection 83.01(1)` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the act or omission is a terrorist activity of paragraph (b) is the answer of section 83.01(1), which was not given
        IF `s 2 terrorist activity: the act or omission would also constitute a terrorist activity referred to in paragraph (b) of the definition terrorist activity in subsection 83.01(1)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "would also constitute a terrorist activity referred to in paragraph (b) of the definition terrorist activity in subsection 83.01(1)"
        IF NOT (null grounds) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is deemed to commit that act or omission in Canada if"

-- The answer that section 83.01(1) "terrorist activity" asks for (PLAN.md section 6, ccc1, seam [T]): both subsections together. Either one deeming the act or omission to have been committed in Canada is enough;
-- JUST FALSE only if both say no in their own words; otherwise NOTHING.
@ref s 7(3.74), (3.75) (a composition of the two subsections: no quotation)
GIVEN `subsection (3.74) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `subsection (3.75) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7 the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` MEANS `ccc1 either of` `subsection (3.74) answers` `subsection (3.75) answers`

-- src:495 | (3.76) and (3.77) [Repealed, 2000, c. 24, s. 42]
@ref s 7(3.76) and (3.77) (src:495-495)
`s 7(3.76) and (3.77) as the text shows them` MEANS "[Repealed, 2000, c. 24, s. 42]"
